@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:architecture] lingui-macros-compiled
Every platform webpack config MUST run `linguiMacroLoader` (`config/webpack_lingui.ts`) on `.ts` and
`.tsx` sources, including the `front` ones, before `ts-loader`, and MUST load `.catalog` imports with
`linguiCatalogRule`. The bundle MUST NOT contain a `@lingui/*/macro` module.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:react] app-root-provides-i18n
Each platform app root (`ChromeApp`, `FirefoxApp`, `FrontApp`) MUST render its whole tree inside an
`I18nProvider` given the `i18n` instance of `@app/lib/i18n/i18n`, itself wrapping a
`SparkleLocaleProvider`, so that front, extension and sparkle components all render in the active
locale.

@cc [owner:Nils-Fedrigo,label:product] extension-follows-user-locale
Once signed in, the extension MUST render in the locale `UserLocaleSync` resolves for the user:
`ProtectedRoute` mounts it, and `ExtensionAuthProvider` MUST pass the `locale` of the workspace
auth context to front's `AuthContext`. Before sign-in, it renders in `DEFAULT_LOCALE`.

@cc [owner:Nils-Fedrigo,label:architecture] extension-catalog
User-visible strings of `platforms/`, `shared/` and `ui/` MUST be written with the Lingui macros
and extracted to the single extension catalog, `extension/locales/{locale}/messages.po`. Code
running outside a React tree (background script, content scripts, page tools) and text sent to
models MUST NOT be translated.
